{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true},{"text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","type":"heading","text":"The four rules","level":2},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"text":" body. Origami ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"text":" means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Switch"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sample and Hold"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onChange"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Flag, don’t fake","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Drag","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Drag","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swami","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Beats","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","abstract":[{"text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","kind":"article"}}}